    note for InspectionQueries "CHANGE 1.0.3: getFormResponsesBySite removes answers that the steward hides.<br>CHANGE 7.0.4: it also returns the question key of each answer.<br>The site page groups answers by that key. There is no separate query."
    note for AuthorizationService "Every protected server action gets the caller from the server session.<br>Admin checks must use a role that the user cannot change. Browser UI checks are not trusted.<br>The role is in app_metadata (role = admin, authenticated = true). RLS reads it too.<br>Today each file has its own copy of the admin check. AuthorizationService replaces these copies."
    note for SiteQueries "US 2.0.8 uses Site, getSiteByName and getFormResponsesBySite.<br>deleteSite removes the Site's SIRs, answers, attachments, homepage images,<br>GPX tracks and other Site-owned rows; their S3 files are also removed."
    note for ExportRoutes "POST /api/export calls createExportJob.<br>GET /api/export/status/[jobId] calls getExportJobStatus.<br>getExportJobStatus returns the URL only to an Admin or the job creator.<br>The ZIP includes inspection images, homepage images, GPX files and completed PDFs."
    note for PdfDataFetcher "CHANGE 7.0.7: removes the answers of options.hiddenQuestionIds.<br>CHANGE 7.0.6: processPdfJob reads the SIRs in batches.<br>The cause of the 50 SIR limit is an open question."
    note for ActivityPointsService "awardActivityPoints reads the caller from the session.<br>It checks the source row belongs to the caller and reads site_id from it."
    note for NewReportPage "NEW 4.0.5: the browser calls iNaturalist. handleSubmit copies<br>each chosen photo to S3 through /api/s3/presign.<br>insertInspectionAttachments writes inat_observation_id.<br>CHANGE 4.0.6: photo identifier is optional and does not block submission.<br>PresignRoute also accepts an empty identifier."
    note for GeocodeRoute "US 6.0.1 AT 4: results are cached and requests stay under 2,500 per day.<br>Open question: where the cache and the daily count are stored."

